==== hyperbricks yaml {!{page}} ====
page:
  - type: hypermedia
  - route: duplicate-item-names

  - content:
      - type: tree

      - text_summary:
          - type: text
          - value: Intro

      - text_summary:
          - type: text
          - value: Summary
==== explainer ====
Duplicate YAML child names are recovered in runtime-load style fixtures.
The first child keeps its name, the second gets a deterministic runtime path.
==== expected json ====
{
  "@order": [
    "content"
  ],
  "@type": "<HYPERMEDIA>",
  "content": {
    "@order": [
      "text_summary",
      "text_summary_2"
    ],
    "@type": "<TREE>",
    "text_summary": {
      "@type": "<TEXT>",
      "value": "Intro"
    },
    "text_summary_2": {
      "@type": "<TEXT>",
      "value": "Summary"
    }
  },
  "route": "duplicate-item-names"
}
==== expected diagnostics ====
[
  {
    "type": "YAML",
    "path": "page.content",
    "key": "text_summary",
    "level": "WARNING",
    "contains": "using \"text_summary_2\" as runtime path"
  }
]
==== expected output ====
<!DOCTYPE html><html><body>IntroSummary</body></html>
